Subject: [PATCH] Warn on Poisson vs NegBinomial2 as a boundary LRT.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

lrtest/anova now detect Poisson ⊂ NegBinomial2 and warn that the extra
sigma is tested at 0. The packaged p-value stays naive chi-square
(issue #304). Use lrt_boundary(; q = 1) for the 50:50 chi-bar p-value
that drmTMB anova() reports for the same pair. Type-I calibration
(#1116, #1118) is left as a methods choice.

Refs #1115
